{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"grammar-lob","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Löb Induction for Grammars"}]},"title_text":"Löb Induction for Grammars","kind":"theorem","taxon":null,"url":"grammar-lob.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","grammar-lob"],["kind","theorem"],["label","Theorem"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"For every grammar "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" and every term "},{"Math":{"src":"phi : class(\"unary\", ▷) A ⊢ A"}},{"Text":", where "},{"Math":{"src":"class(\"unary\", ▷)"}},{"Text":" is the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"grammar-later","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"later on grammars"}]}},{"Text":", there is a unique global parse "},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"löb\") thin phi : ⊤ ⊢ A"}},{"Text":" with"}]},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"löb\") thin phi = phi ∘ sans(\"next\") thin (sans(\"löb\") thin phi) ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Here "},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"next\") thin t : ⊤ ⊢ class(\"unary\", ▷) A"}},{"Text":" restricts a global parse "},{"Math":{"src":"t"}},{"Text":" to every proper suffix."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The proof is recursion on the length of the string. At "},{"Math":{"src":"v"}},{"Text":", the parses already built at the proper suffixes of "},{"Math":{"src":"v"}},{"Text":" form an element of "},{"Math":{"src":"(class(\"unary\", ▷) A) thin v"}},{"Text":", and "},{"Math":{"src":"phi"}},{"Text":" turns it into a parse at "},{"Math":{"src":"v"}},{"Text":". Uniqueness is "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"lob-family","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"Löb for families"}]}},{"Text":" over the proper-suffix order. In the Agda, "},{"RawSpan":{"lang":null,"text":"lob"}},{"Text":" in "},{"RawSpan":{"lang":null,"text":"Grammar/Later/Base.agda"}},{"Text":" is this recursion, done by well-founded induction on length."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"To prove an entailment "},{"Math":{"src":"B ⊢ C"}},{"Text":" this way, apply Löb to "},{"Math":{"src":"A = B class(\"binary\", =>) C"}},{"Text":". The hypothesis "},{"Math":{"src":"class(\"unary\", ▷) (B class(\"binary\", =>) C)"}},{"Text":" is the induction hypothesis at every proper suffix. It becomes usable once a non-nullable grammar has been consumed. If "},{"Math":{"src":"ε class(\"binary\", \\&) B ⊢ ⊥"}},{"Text":", then"}]},{"Math":{"src":"(B ⊗ ⊤) class(\"binary\", \\&) class(\"unary\", ▷) A ⊢ B ⊗ A"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"because a parse of "},{"Math":{"src":"B ⊗ ⊤"}},{"Text":" over "},{"Math":{"src":"v"}},{"Text":" splits "},{"Math":{"src":"v = x class(\"binary\", mono(\"++\")) u"}},{"Text":" with "},{"Math":{"src":"x"}},{"Text":" non-empty, so "},{"Math":{"src":"u class(\"relation\", ⊏) v"}},{"Text":". This is "},{"RawSpan":{"lang":null,"text":"▷-app-NE"}},{"Text":" in "},{"RawSpan":{"lang":null,"text":"Grammar/Later/Properties.agda"}},{"Text":". Induction on a Kleene star is the standard use."}]}]}}}]}}
